ows the layers of the Earth. Tap the crust.', null, 'The crust is the thin outer layer of the Earth shown at the rim of the cross-section.', '{"mode":"tap","image":{"alt":"Cross-section of the Earth with labelled concentric layers, crust on the outside.","ref":"question-media/science/earth-space/earth-layers.png","role":"diagram","width":400,"height":400},"hotspots":[{"x":50,"y":6,"id":"h1","label":"The crust","radius":12}],"imageWidth":400,"imageHeight":400,"schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"mode":"tap","requiredHotspots":["h1"]}', '[{"text":"It is the outermost layer you would walk on.","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:earth-space','subtopic:earth-structure'], 7, 9, 2, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:13.005+00', '2026-08-17 21:30:19.414+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:30:18.766Z","submittedAt":"2026-08-17T21:30:18.148Z","reviewerAdminId":"a051d17f-a273-4ffb-b79f-b1bc435322c6","submittedByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"feedback":{"correct":"Correct — the explanation above shows why.","incorrect":"Not quite. Read the explanation below and try again."},"authoring":{"authorType":"import","contentHash":"1833893b34ee6bb0146332735474931397e5b1e36299ec78f13fe9aad80245cc","authorSource":"stem-quest-task-5.14-batch-1-science","createdByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"objective":"Identify the Earth’s crust in a diagram."}'), (389, 1, 3, 7, 'Choose the next stage: Seed, Sprout, Seedling, …', null, 'A seed grows into a sprout, then a seedling, then a full plant.', '{"sequence":[{"id":"e1","text":"Seed"},{"id":"e2","text":"Sprout"},{"id":"e3","text":"Seedling"}],"candidates":[{"id":"c1","text":"Plant"},{"id":"c2","text":"Root"},{"id":"c3","text":"Fruit"},{"id":"c4","text":"Petal"}],"interaction":"complete-sequence","schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"rule":"The growth of a plant.","type":"candidate","acceptableIds":["c1"]}', '[{"text":"Each stage is bigger and more developed.","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:life','subtopic:plants-animals'], 7, 9, 1, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:13.591+00', '2026-08-17 21:27:03.477+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:02.974Z","submittedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:02.479Z","reviewerAdminId":"a051d17f-a273-4ffb-b79f-b1bc435322c6","submittedByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"feedback":{"correct":"Correct — the explanation above shows why.","incorrect":"Not quite. Read the explanation below and try again."},"authoring":{"authorType":"import","contentHash":"669a3a98a62bda3784e01bfbb03b6dde9e780b8157b638e8b6db1512764bf27a","authorSource":"stem-quest-task-5.14-batch-1-science","createdByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"objective":"Order the growth stages of a plant."}'), (390, 1, 3, 8, 'Memorise each force with its effect, then match the pairs.', null, 'A force is a push or pull, gravity pulls downward, friction slows motion and magnetism attracts iron.', '{"cards":[{"id":"c1","text":"Force"},{"id":"c2","text":"Push or pull"},{"id":"c3","text":"Gravity"},{"id":"c4","text":"Pulls downward"},{"id":"c5","text":"Friction"},{"id":"c6","text":"Slows motion"},{"id":"c7","text":"Magnetism"},{"id":"c8","text":"Attracts iron"}],"shuffle":true,"deckType":"pairs","recallPrompt":"Remember each force with its effect.","revealSeconds":12,"schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"groups":[{"cardIds":["c1","c2"],"groupId":"g1"},{"cardIds":["c3","c4"],"groupId":"g2"},{"cardIds":["c5","c6"],"groupId":"g3"},{"cardIds":["c7","c8"],"groupId":"g4"}]}', '[{"text":"Each pair links a force to its effect.","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:physics','subtopic:forces-motion'], 7, 9, 3, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:14.202+00', '2026-08-17 21:27:05.136+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:04.