 solution of pH 3 is how many times more acidic than a solution of pH 5?","inputMode":"numeric","answerFormat":"integer","schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"type":"exact","value":100}', '[{"text":"Each step of 1 on the pH scale is a tenfold change.","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:chemistry','subtopic:acids-bases'], 7, 9, 4, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:15.392+00', '2026-08-17 21:27:08.201+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:07.612Z","submittedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:07.122Z","reviewerAdminId":"a051d17f-a273-4ffb-b79f-b1bc435322c6","submittedByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"feedback":{"correct":"Correct — the explanation above shows why.","incorrect":"Not quite. Read the explanation below and try again."},"authoring":{"authorType":"import","contentHash":"5ccd045a06287cf3b78c3cdfe062ce18bf21d393d0ba1cf5cb361cb0dea8b8c7","authorSource":"stem-quest-task-5.14-batch-1-science","createdByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"objective":"Compare acidity using the pH scale."}'), (393, 1, 3, 9, 'Choose the safest action for a chemical spill.', null, 'The safe response to any unknown spill is to alert a teacher, who will direct the correct cleanup.', '{"decisions":[{"id":"d1","text":"What should you do first?","options":[{"id":"opt_tell","text":"Tell the teacher immediately","outcomeText":"The teacher assesses the spill and directs the safe cleanup — the correct choice.","nextDecision":null},{"id":"opt_hand","text":"Wipe it up with your hand","outcomeText":"Touching an unknown liquid can be dangerous.","nextDecision":null},{"id":"opt_sink","text":"Pour it down the sink","outcomeText":"Unknown chemicals must never be poured away without instructions.","nextDecision":null}]}],"scenarioText":"During a lab experiment you accidentally knock over a beaker and a clear liquid spills across the bench.","entryDecision":"d1","schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"optima