 springs, cables); compression pushes it together (columns, cushions, walls).', '{"items":[{"id":"i1","label":"Rope holding a hanging weight"},{"id":"i2","label":"Column supporting a roof"},{"id":"i3","label":"Stretched spring"},{"id":"i4","label":"Squeezed cushion"},{"id":"i5","label":"Bridge cable under load"},{"id":"i6","label":"Bottom brick of a wall"}],"shuffle":true,"categories":[{"id":"c_t","label":"Tension"},{"id":"c_c","label":"Compression"}],"schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"assignments":[{"itemId":"i1","categoryId":"c_t"},{"itemId":"i2","categoryId":"c_c"},{"itemId":"i3","categoryId":"c_t"},{"itemId":"i4","categoryId":"c_c"},{"itemId":"i5","categoryId":"c_t"},{"itemId":"i6","categoryId":"c_c"}]}', '[{"text":"Is the material being stretched or squashed?","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:materials-structures','subtopic:forces-in-structures'], 7, 9, 3, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:34.352+00', '2026-08-17 21:27:48.852+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:48.362Z","submittedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:47.817Z","reviewerAdminId":"a051d17f-a273-4ffb-b79f-b1bc435322c6","submittedByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"feedback":{"correct":"Correct — the explanation above shows why.","incorrect":"Not quite. Read the explanation below and try again."},"authoring":{"authorType":"import","contentHash":"30e1df32be08c3cf43e3670b96235a1a498628f9450b3dc91e656fac4048d6f1","authorSource":"stem-quest-task-5.14-batch-1-engineering","createdByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"objective":"Distinguish tension from compression."}'), (423, 3, 13, 5, 'The steps a team follows from a problem to a final solution are called the ___ process.', null, 'The design process covers defining, researching, designing, prototyping and testing.', '{"blanks":[{"id":"b1","type":"text","label":"process","maxLength":18}],"template":"The steps a team follows from a problem to a final solution are called the ___ process.","schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"answers":[{"type":"text","blankId":"b1","accepted":["design","design process","engineering design"]}]}', '[{"text":"It starts with a problem and ends with a tested solution.","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:design-process','subtopic:define-problem'], 7, 9, 2, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:34.981+00', '2026-08-17 21:27:50.411+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:49.860Z","submittedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:49.348Z","reviewerAdminId":"a051d17f-a273-4ffb-b79f-b1bc435322c6","submittedByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"feedback":{"correct":"Correct — the explanation above shows why.","incorrect":"Not quite. Read the explanation below and try again."},"authoring":{"authorType":"import","contentHash":"c2e8c1cfff6cc0e4cb021bc7749b59a7ac7fe3ba5136fdd9f018224ef5732c36","authorSource":"stem-quest-task-5.14-batch-1-engineering","createdByAdminId":"ed8843ee-f598-4966-aae1-f5ebf481af58"},"objective":"Name the engineering design process."}'), (424, 3, 13, 3, 'Arrange the design process steps in order.', null, 'Define the problem → research → design → build a prototype → test and evaluate.', '{"items":[{"id":"o1","label":"Build a prototype"},{"id":"o2","label":"Define the problem"},{"id":"o3","label":"Test and evaluate"},{"id":"o4","label":"Design a solution"},{"id":"o5","label":"Research ideas"}],"shuffle":true,"schemaVersion":"1.0"}', '{"order":["o2","o5","o4","o1","o3"]}', '[{"text":"Building comes after designing but before testing.","level":1}]', ARRAY['topic:design-process','subtopic:define-problem'], 7, 9, 2, 100, null, 'published', false, 1, '2026-08-17 21:19:35.679+00', '2026-08-17 21:27:51.91+00', '{"review":{"note":"Batch 1 content-bank question approved","state":"approved","version":1,"reviewedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:51.381Z","submittedAt":"2026-08-17T21:27:50.899Z","reviewerAdminId":